From 6496c76b554a482c6c59bfa215a5d531a0590664 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: g1-door <g1-door@local>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:53:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] door: optional yaw disturbance of the pelvis during the
 arm-only stage and optional wall and door cover depth (env.config.yaw_disturb
 rotates the robot root about the world vertical axis through the pelvis
 before physics at every step by the difference between a cosine ramp from 0
 to amp_deg over dur_s starting at start_s and what was already added, keeping
 the joint angles, the height and the tilt and rotating the linear and angular
 velocity, toward the lever side by default (sign follows door_open_lr),
 redrawn per episode, also drawn in __init__ because the first reset runs
 before it exists; on 11-11 the real stock legs turned the body by +10 to +25
 deg 1.5 to 2.0 s into the arm-only stage just before the hand came down and
 the hand landed 9 to 14 cm toward the lever pivot; robot_root_states is read
 as xyzw and written back as wxyz; DoorSpawnerCfg.wall_front_out and
 cover_front_out put the front face of the side and top walls and of the
 covers that far in front of the panel face, keeping the back face and drawing
 no random numbers so the same seed builds the same doors, the real UIS Room 4
 being about 0.01 and 0.03 m against 0.05 and 0.06 m, used by the new task
 door_en1154_g13_shaped_left_weight_realwall generated by
 make_door_scenarios.py; default off = unchanged) (11-11)

